      "funding_type": "rental assistance",
      "typical_award_size": "HACM administers Housing Choice Vouchers countywide (including Salinas) with a Housing Choice Voucher Administrative Plan effective September 28, 2026 that provides for competitive selection of PBV proposals (Chapter 17) and noncompetitive selection of PHA-owned units; recent PBV properties include Alfred Diaz-Infante Apartments (Salinas, 2024 list), One Parkside (Salinas), Villa del Monte (Monterey Peninsula), Magnolia Place Senior II (Greenfield) and South County sites; the last public PBV request for proposals was in 2020. The HACM Development Corporation develops and co-owns housing (Haciendas 1-4 and Tynan Village in Salinas, Rippling River in Carmel Valley with a 2006 County HOME and CDBG loan of $1,262,500, Benito Farm Labor Center in Soledad, Oak Park in Paso Robles) and in May 2026 reaffirmed Milestone Housing Group as development partner for its Greenfield sites (Resolution 3160).",
